## 3. Backend installation (Cloudflare Worker)

Open a terminal in the **backend** folder:

```bash
cd backend
npm install
```

What this installs:

| Package | Role |
|---|---|
| `cheerio` | HTML parsing for the scraper |
| `firebase` | Official SDK used by `FirestoreRepository` (Node/tests) |
| `vitest` | Test runner (`npm test`) |
| `wrangler` | Cloudflare Workers CLI (dev server, deploy, secrets, cron) |

Verify Wrangler is available:

```bash
npx wrangler --version
```

### Project files you will configure

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `backend/src/worker.js` | Fetch router + scheduled (cron) handler |
| `backend/wrangler.toml` | Worker name, entrypoint, **cron schedule** (no variables — `API_KEY` is a secret, see §12) |
| `backend/src/config/firebaseConfig.js` | Firebase project credentials (defaults for REST repo) |

