## 4. Environment variables — local

### 4.1 `wrangler.toml` (worker config — no variables)

Current file:

```toml
name = "hacker-news-scraper"
main = "src/worker.js"
compatibility_date = "2026-09-01"

[triggers]
crons = ["0 * * * *"]
```

> **Cron note:** the trigger is a **fixed hourly wake** (`0 * * * *`). The real scrape frequency is chosen in the **UI** and stored in Firestore (`frequency_hours` + `last_run_hour`) — see [§13](#13-cloudflare-cron-triggers-scheduled-jobs).

> **No `[vars] API_KEY`:** the file intentionally has **no** `[vars]` section. A `[vars]` binding with the same name as an existing secret is rejected at deploy (`10053`). The key lives in `.dev.vars` (local) and in the Cloudflare secret (production, §12).

| Variable | Required | Where it lives | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `API_KEY` | **Yes** | `backend/.dev.vars` (local) · Cloudflare **secret** (prod) | Server-only secret used to sign session tokens; also accepted directly as legacy credential (`x-api-key: <API_KEY>` or `Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>`). Browsers use short-lived tokens from `POST /api/session` instead. If missing at runtime the Worker returns **500** (fail-closed). |
| `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` | No | `firebaseConfig.js` default; secret to override | Overrides Firebase project id. Default comes from `firebaseConfig.js` (`test-2eb64`). |
| `FIREBASE_API_KEY` | No | `firebaseConfig.js` default; secret to override | Overrides Firebase web API key. Default from `firebaseConfig.js`. |

**Local behavior:** `npx wrangler dev` automatically loads `backend/.dev.vars`; production loads the secrets set with `wrangler secret put` (§12).

### 4.2 Local secrets file (`.dev.vars`) — required for local dev

Create `backend/.dev.vars` (git-ignored, never committed):

```bash
# backend/.dev.vars  (loaded only by wrangler dev, never deployed as file)
API_KEY=your-local-secret-key
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=test-2eb64
FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSy...your-key...
```

Then **match** the same `API_KEY` in the frontend (see §7).

> `.dev.vars` is read by `wrangler dev` only. For production use Cloudflare dashboard/CLI secrets (§12).

