## 5. Run backend locally

```bash
cd backend
npx wrangler dev --port 8787
```

Expected console output (simplified):

```
⛅️ wrangler x.x.x
Your Worker has access to the following bindings:
  env.API_KEY ("hn-scraper-...")   Environment Variable   local
⎔ Starting local server...
wget http://127.0.0.1:8787
```

| Endpoint | Method | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/api/session` | POST | **None** (rate-limited 60/min/IP) | Issue a 15-minute bearer token |
| `/` | GET | Token / API key | Health / service info |
| `/api/entries?filter=NO_FILTER` | GET | Token / API key | Scrape + optional filter + audit |
| `/api/entries?filter=MORE_THAN_5_WORDS_BY_COMMENTS` | GET | Token / API key | Business filter 1 |
| `/api/entries?filter=LESS_OR_EQUAL_5_WORDS_BY_POINTS` | GET | Token / API key | Business filter 2 |
| `/api/scrape` | GET | Token / API key | Scrape + save to `entries_cache` |
| `/api/config` | GET / PUT | Token / API key | Read / update cron configuration |
| `OPTIONS` | * | **None** | CORS preflight |

**Stop the server:** `Ctrl+C` in that terminal.

