## 10. Run automated tests

### Backend (Vitest)

```bash
cd backend
npm test
```

Variants:

```bash
npm run test:watch
npm run test:firestore      # real Firestore integration
npm run test:web            # real news.ycombinator.com smoke test
npx vitest run tests/worker.test.js --reporter=verbose
```

> Integration tests write to the real Firebase project and hit the live HN site — network required.
> The scraper prefers the `news.ycombinator.com` HTML source and automatically falls back to the official HN API (`hacker-news.firebaseio.com`) when the HTML fetch fails (network error / HTTP 419) or parses to 0 entries; `HackerNewsScraper.test.js` covers all three triggers with mocked fetchers.

### Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm run lint
npm run build
```

Both must succeed before considering the install healthy.

