## 11. Deploy backend to Cloudflare (production)

### 11.1 Log in to Cloudflare

```bash
cd backend
npx wrangler login
```

A browser window opens; authorize the CLI.

### 11.2 Confirm `wrangler.toml` before deploy

- `name` — Worker subdomain name (e.g. `hacker-news-scraper` → `hacker-news-scraper.<account>.workers.dev`).
- `main = "src/worker.js"` — entry file.
- `[triggers] crons` — schedule (see §13).
- **No `[vars]` section** — `API_KEY` must be a secret (§12); a `[vars]` binding colliding with an existing secret fails the deploy (`10053`).

### 11.3 Deploy

```bash
npx wrangler deploy
```

Wrangler prints the **production URL**, e.g.:

```
Deployed hacker-news-scraper triggers (cron)
  https://hacker-news-scraper.<account>.workers.dev
```

Record this URL — it becomes `VITE_API_BASE_URL` for the frontend.

### 11.4 Redeploy after code changes

```bash
npx wrangler deploy
```

Cron schedules defined in `wrangler.toml` are updated automatically on deploy.

