## 14. Deploy frontend to production

Any static host works (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify, Vercel, S3…). Example with **Cloudflare Pages**:

```bash
cd frontend

# 1) Set production env (the deployed Worker URL; no API key — the UI gets session tokens)
export VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://hacker-news-scraper.<account>.workers.dev"

# 2) Lint + build
npm run lint
npm run build          # outputs dist/

# 3) Deploy dist/ (Pages Git integration or wrangler pages)
npx wrangler pages deploy dist --project-name=scropcombinator
```

Dashboard alternative:

1. **Workers & Pages** → **Create** → **Pages** → upload/`dist` or connect Git.
2. Build command: `npm run build` · Output directory: `dist`.
3. Define Environment variable `VITE_API_BASE_URL` in Pages **Settings → Environment variables** (Production + Preview) **before** build. No API key variable exists anymore.

CORS: the Worker already returns `access-control-allow-origin: *`, so the Pages domain can call the API.

