## 16. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` on `:8787` | Wrangler not running / crashed | Restart `npx wrangler dev --port 8787`; check for startup TypeError |
| Worker fails: *Incorrect type for map entry …* | A non-handler **named export** in `worker.js` | Export only handlers; keep constants local (e.g. `NO_FILTER`) |
| HTTP **500** `API key is not configured` | `API_KEY` secret missing (prod) or `.dev.vars` missing (local) | `npx wrangler secret put API_KEY` (prod) or create `backend/.dev.vars` (local) — never `[vars]`, that collides with the secret (`10053`) |
| HTTP **401** from UI | Worker restarted with a rotated `API_KEY`, or `POST /api/session` failing (429 rate limit) | Tokens are renewed automatically (1× retry on 401); if it persists check Worker logs and wait up to 1 min if you hit the 60 req/min session limit |
| UI loads but logs empty | Firestore rules block read, or no data yet | Allow read for `usage_logs` in rules; trigger a filter run |
| Scrape 500 from Worker | Both HTML **and** official HN API failed | Error message shows `Failed to fetch Hacker News from HTML and API. HTML: … API: …`; check network / HN status in Worker logs |
| Scrape works but logs show `419 Sorry` from `news.ycombinator.com` | HN blocks Cloudflare IPs (HTML source) | Expected in prod — the scraper auto-falls back to `hacker-news.firebaseio.com`; look for `[scraper] … using official HN API` and `lastSource: "api"` |
| Cron never runs in prod | Trigger not deployed, `cron_enabled` false, or `frequency_hours` not elapsed (`frequency_not_reached`) | Redeploy; save UI schedule (`cron_enabled: true`); wait `frequency_hours` since `last_run_hour` |
| Cron does not run in `wrangler dev` | Expected — local crons are manual | `curl http://127.0.0.1:8787/cdn-cgi/local/scheduled` |
| Env changes ignored | Vite caches env at process start | Restart `npm run dev` / rebuild |
| Firebase SDK errors inside Worker | SDK unsupported on Workers | Runtime uses `FirestoreRestRepository` (REST) — expected on CF |

### Useful log commands

```bash
# Live Worker logs (production)
npx wrangler tail

# Local logs are printed in the wrangler dev terminal
```

